---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout
  title="Nextfuse: Running Nextflow® in Domino | KSM Technology Partners"
  description="Nextfuse streamlines Nextflow® pipelines inside Domino — per-process compute allocation, real-time pipeline visualization, and GxP-grade audit trails."
>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Hero
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="overline">Solutions — Life Sciences</span>
    <h1>Nextfuse: Running Nextflow® in Domino</h1>
    <p>
      Nextfuse bridges Nextflow®'s pipeline execution model with Domino's enterprise
      compute platform — giving bioinformaticians the scale,
      traceability, and control their work demands.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href="../contact" class="btn">Talk to an Expert</a>
      <a href="https://nextfuse.ksmpartners.com" class="btn btn-ghost">Explore the Documentation</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Intro: What is Nextfuse
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section nf-section-intro">
    <div class="nf-intro">
      <div>
        <h2>Managed compute for your Nextflow® pipelines.</h2>
        <p class="intro-para">
          Domino gives life sciences teams browser access, abundant storage, customized compute environments, and Git repository integration. Nextflow® gives them the pipeline orchestration language their workflows for processing high-memory, high-compute, long-running tasks in parallel. Nextfuse makes them work together — executing each Nextflow® process as its own
          Domino job, without modification, with precisely the CPU and memory it needs.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because Domino runs on cloud-based Kubernetes, your Nextflow® workloads
          scale on demand. No continuously-running, costly VMs. No overprovisioning to handle peak load.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="nf-partner-block">
        <div class="partner-label">Proud Domino Data Lab Partner</div>
        <p>
          KSM helps customers through every phase of Domino implementation — from
          environment capacity planning and installation through custom compute
          environment definition, Git integration, and load and scalability testing. Whether for bioinformatics, biostatistics, or other life sciences usages, we have the accelerators and experience to get you up and running fast and with full GxP compliance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Accelerators
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale" id="accelerators">
    <div class="section nf-section-accels">
      <span class="overline">The Nextfuse Family</span>
      <h2>Two accelerators. One fully-integrated solution.</h2>
      <p class="intro-para">
        Each accelerator in the Nextfuse family solves a distinct challenge in
        running production Nextflow® workloads inside Domino. Together they cover
        execution and observability.
      </p>

      <div class="nf-accelerators">

        <!-- Nextfuse Core -->
        <div class="nf-accel-card">
          <div class="nf-accel-header nf-accel-header--core">
            <p class="nf-accel-tagline">Pipeline execution as Domino jobs</p>
          </div>
          <div class="nf-accel-body">
            <img
              src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/NextFuse-Logo-Blue.svg`}
              alt="Nextfuse"
              class="nf-accel-logo"
            />
            <p>
              Nextfuse streamlines Nextflow® pipelines inside Domino, executing each
              process as a Domino job with a tailored compute environment. Perfect for
              bioinformaticians and biostatisticians who want Nextflow®'s orchestration
              with Domino's infrastructure.
            </p>
            <ul class="nf-feature-list">
              <li>Per-process CPU and memory allocation — no more one-size-fits-all compute</li>
              <li>Browser-based access, abundant storage, and Git integration via Domino</li>
              <li>Kubernetes-backed auto-scaling eliminates the need for standing VMs, scaling up to meet surges in demands and scaling down when not needed to reduce costs</li>
              <li>Drop-in fit for pipelines already written in Nextflow® DSL</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Nextfuse Monitor -->
        <div class="nf-accel-card">
          <div class="nf-accel-header nf-accel-header--monitor">
            <p class="nf-accel-tagline">Real-time pipeline visibility</p>
          </div>
          <div class="nf-accel-body">
            <img
              src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}images/NextFuse-Monitor-Logo.svg`}
              alt="Nextfuse Monitor"
              class="nf-accel-logo nf-accel-logo--monitor"
            />
            <p>
              Nextflow® pipelines generate dozens of Domino jobs that are hard to
              differentiate in the standard jobs UI. Nextfuse Monitor understands
              Nextflow® execution graphs and visualizes the full pipeline in real-time —
              with Nextflow®-assigned process names, not opaque job IDs.
            </p>
            <ul class="nf-feature-list">
              <li>Real-time DAG visualization as processes complete</li>
              <li>Processes displayed with their Nextflow®-assigned names for intuitive debugging</li>
              <li>Domino API integration surfaces CPU usage, memory, and log details per job</li>
              <li>Domino Datasets API access for web-based browsing of interim pipeline artifacts</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       CTA
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section-pale">
    <div class="section nf-cta">
      <div>
        <h2>A Drop-In Solution for Your Nextflow® Workloads</h2>
        <p>
          Nextfuse gives you all the safety, security, and reproducibility of Domino computing environments without having to rewrite your Nextflow® workflows. Check out the documentation at <a href="https://nextfuse.ksmpartners.com" target="_blank">https://nextfuse.ksmpartners.com</a> to learn more, and then click the button below to schedule a conversation with a KSM expert.
        </p>
        <a href="../contact" class="btn">Schedule a Conversation</a>
      </div>
      <div class="nf-cta-aside">
        <div class="nf-cta-stat">
          <span>KSM Technology Partners has over</span>
          <strong>23 years</strong>
          <span>building solutions for all phases of pharmaceutical research and development.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Trademark footnote
       ============================================================ -->
  <div class="section nf-footnote">
    <p>Nextflow® is a registered trademark of Seqera Labs, S.L. Use of this trademark on this site does not imply endorsement of Nextfuse by Seqera Labs, S.L.</p>
  </div>

</PageLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Section spacing overrides ─────────────────────────────────── */
  .nf-section-intro { padding-bottom: var(--space-8) !important; }
  .nf-section-accels { padding-top: var(--space-8) !important; }

  /* ── Intro layout ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .nf-intro {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3fr 2fr;
    gap: 4rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .nf-intro { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; }
  }

  .nf-partner-block {
    background: var(--color-primary);
    color: #fff;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .partner-label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .nf-partner-block p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Accelerator cards ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .nf-accelerators {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .nf-accelerators { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  .nf-accel-card {
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow:
      0 2px 6px rgba(0, 77, 113, 0.06),
      0 8px 24px rgba(0, 77, 113, 0.08);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  .nf-accel-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    box-shadow:
      0 4px 12px rgba(0, 77, 113, 0.1),
      0 16px 36px rgba(0, 77, 113, 0.12);
  }

  .nf-accel-header {
    padding: 0.875rem 1.75rem;
  }

  .nf-accel-header--core    { background: var(--color-primary); }
  .nf-accel-header--monitor { background: #0a6e9a; }

  .nf-accel-tagline {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #7ecfee;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .nf-accel-logo {
    display: block;
    width: 260px;
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  /* Monitor logo is taller (includes "MONITOR" subtitle) — constrain width slightly */
  .nf-accel-logo--monitor {
    width: 240px;
  }

  .nf-accel-body {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .nf-accel-body p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #555;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .nf-feature-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .nf-feature-list li {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #444;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .nf-feature-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.5em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* ── CTA ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .nf-cta {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3fr 2fr;
    gap: 4rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .nf-cta { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; }
  }

  .nf-cta h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .nf-cta p {
    color: #555;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .nf-cta-aside {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .nf-cta-stat {
    background: var(--color-primary);
    color: #fff;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: center;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .nf-cta-stat span {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,0.75);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .nf-cta-stat strong {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  /* ── Shared helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .intro-para {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #555;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .nf-footnote {
    padding-top: 0 !important;
  }

  .nf-footnote p {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: #999;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .mt-2 { margin-top: 2rem; }

  .overline {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
